      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i've been trying out this box breathing thing (4 in, 4 hold, 4 out, 4 hold) to help with stress but i wanted to know the actual science behind it. like how does that specific timing actually affect my nervous system or cortisol?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing, or 4-4-4-4 breathing, can help calm the nervous system by promoting parasympathetic activity, allowing your body to relax. By taking slow, deep breaths, it lowers cortisol levels, reducing the \"fight or flight\" response and lowering stress. The 4-in, 4-hold, 4-out, 4-hold pattern helps maintain an balance of oxygen levels and CO2, aiding in stress relief. Consistent practice helps improve overall relaxation and stress management.",
